text:
Maria (docs): quick heads-up — planning a gentle deprecation for the v1 /invoke path. goal: announce with a short migration snippet and a compatibility note so customers see no sudden break. thinking June 15 rollout window.

Kevin (sdk): I can author a tiny v2 snippet that maps the old params to the new ones. will keep it <=10 lines and add a comment about token behavior. ping me the exact fields you want preserved.

Tara (prod): FYI production will need the fallback policy documented: how requests fall back to model-alias when the exact model version is missing. also include a canary flag example for Dedicated.

Maria (docs): good call. target content: 1) short user-facing notice, 2) example request mapping (js + curl), 3) deprecation schedule + links to SDK migration snippets, 4) rollback steps. can someone check legal/comms language? Evan?

Evan (legal): I'll sanity check the wording for "deprecate" vs "sunset" language. prefer "deprecated" with a clear end-of-life date and a migration window. no legal objections to the plan but will review the notice text before send.

Kevin (sdk): draft snippet below — lightweight, shows old -> new param mapping. please review for correctness and edgecases.

Kevin (sdk): ```js
// v1 -> v2 minimal mapping
// old: POST /v1/invoke { model: "rwd-small", input: "hey" }
// new: POST /v2/responses { model: "rwd-small@v2", input: "hey" }
const v1 = { model: "rwd-small", input: "hello" };
const v2 = {
  model: v1.model + "@v2",
  input: v1.input,
  // preserve top-level metadata
  metadata: v1.metadata || {}
};
// send v2 request via Redwood client
client.responses.create(v2);
```

Maria (docs): nice and simple. can we add a one-line note about embed behavior changing for alias swaps? also include a sample curl for non-js users.

Kevin (sdk): added curl + one-liner note below.

Kevin (sdk): ```bash
curl -X POST https://api.redwood.ai/v2/responses \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $REDWOOD_KEY" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"model":"rwd-small@v2","input":"hello"}'
```

Kevin (sdk): Note: if you previously relied on implicit aliasing, v2 requires explicit model@version when pinning exact behavior. otherwise the platform will route to the alias and you may see embedding dimension differences.

Tara (prod): for the canary example we should show a traffic-split header and fallback policy. something like X-Canary: true and a 503->fallback to alias mapping snippet.

Maria (docs): agreed. I'll draft the canary paragraph and the fallback table. also planning a tiny checkbox list for customers to verify before migration: tokenization sanity check, embed dims, and API key scopes.

docs-bot: PR opened -> https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/5421 (draft: deprecate v1 invoke, includes snippets and rollback).

Maria (docs): thanks bot. @Kevin can you drop the finalized snippet into the PR and @Evan I'll DM you the notice text for quick review.

Evan (legal): will review in the next 24 hours. please add an internal note about enterprise customers that are on dedicated contracts — we'll coordinate the timeline with account teams.

Kevin (sdk): adding snippet to PR shortly. leaving a small comment about edge case when `metadata` contains binary blobs.

Tara (prod): reminder — update the Console deprecation banner content and the SDK changelog entry when PR merges. I'll schedule the banner date for June 10 to give a 5-day heads-up.

Maria (docs): perfect. action items: Kevin -> finalize PR snippet (due EOD), Evan -> legal review (24h), Tara -> banner + fallback doc (by June 1), Maria -> publish notice + small migration guide (by June 5). I'll follow up with a short Slack announcement draft for the dev-community channel. :memo: :wave:
